It's still potentially game-ending -- if the Quest Leader kills you
before you can get away, this will end your game just as surely as if
he'd expelled you, and more immediately.  And if he kills you while
you're trying to pacify him... etc.

That's part of the appeal, really.  Killing the Leader or pacifying
him, either way -- but the player isn't just left to wander aimlessly,
trying to complete a game he doesn't necessarily realize he can't
finish.  The banishment message refers to the Bell, but a lot of games
have a tendency to have your characters told they can 'never' do things,
and yet the game has provided a way for the character to indeed, do that
thing if he just looks hard enough.

...Like the message that started this whole thread, in fact!  :)

